{"content_hash": "29361b1da3ff55f0", "version_id": 143, "article_id": 15, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "US Death Row Inmate Christa Pike Awake and Speaking After Failed Execution", "title_zh": "美国死囚克里斯塔·派克处决失败后苏醒并能说话", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8kgezxn54qko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/226c/live/7221efd0-c1c9-11f1-b8a9-47f21beea0a3.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 257, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Christa Pike survived a failed lethal injection in Tennessee. Now her lawyers say she is conscious and speaking, which experts call unprecedented.", "lead_zh": "克里斯塔·派克在田纳西州一次失败的注射死刑中活了下来。现在她的律师说她已恢复意识并能说话，专家称这史无前例。", "preview": "Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate, is now conscious and speaking after she survived a failed execution last week. Although she re", "preview_zh": "50岁的死囚克里斯塔·派克上周在一次失败的处决中幸存，现在已恢复意识并能说话。尽管她仍处于危急状态，但她的律师周二表示，她正在医院接受治疗，戴着手铐。她因1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默而被判处死刑。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 133, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/audio/15/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 102.975, "size_bytes": 621648, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 301, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/data/versions/143.json", "paragraphs": ["Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate, is now conscious and speaking after she survived a failed execution last week. Although she remains in critical condition, her lawyers said on Tuesday that she is receiving medical care while handcuffed in a hospital. She was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995.", "Last Wednesday, Pike survived two failed lethal injections in Tennessee. Because the chemicals did not work as planned, she was taken to hospital, where she stayed unconscious for days. Experts say she is believed to be the only person ever to survive a lethal injection. Her lawyers called her recovery 'medically unprecedented'.", "Deborah Denno, a criminologist at Fordham Law School, said she was 'absolutely astonished' that Pike is awake. In seven other cases, prisoners survived because executioners could not inject anything into their veins. However, Pike is the only person who actually received a toxin. 'This has never happened before,' Denno said.", "Authorities have not said whether they will try to execute Pike again, and they have not explained what went wrong. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee has suspended all executions for the rest of the year, and the state's prison chief plans to resign. Pike's attorneys will appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday.", "Dr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said most people die from lethal injection. He warned that many unknowns remain, such as how much pentobarbital entered her system and what her recovery will look like. 'I would not say all the big risks are behind her,' he noted."], "paragraphs_zh": ["50岁的死囚克里斯塔·派克上周在一次失败的处决中幸存，现在已恢复意识并能说话。尽管她仍处于危急状态，但她的律师周二表示，她正在医院接受治疗，戴着手铐。她因1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默而被判处死刑。", "上周三，派克在田纳西州两次注射死刑失败后幸存。由于化学药物没有按计划起作用，她被送往医院，昏迷了数天。专家称，她被认为是唯一一个在注射死刑后幸存的人。她的律师称她的康复是“医学上史无前例的”。", "福特汉姆法学院的犯罪学家黛博拉·丹诺说，她对派克清醒并能说话感到“绝对震惊”。在另外七起案件中，囚犯幸存是因为行刑者无法将药物注入他们的静脉。然而，派克是唯一实际接受了毒素的人。丹诺说：“这种情况从未发生过。”", "当局尚未表示是否会再次处决派克，也没有解释出了什么问题。田纳西州州长比尔·李已暂停今年剩余时间的所有处决，该州监狱负责人计划辞职。派克的律师将于周三在纳什维尔出庭。", "为派克辩护团队提供咨询的麻醉师乔尔·齐沃特博士说，大多数人会死于注射死刑。他警告说，仍有许多未知因素，例如有多少戊巴比妥进入了她的体内，以及她的康复情况会如何。他指出：“我不会说所有重大风险都已过去。”"], "body": "Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate, is now conscious and speaking after she survived a failed execution last week. Although she remains in critical condition, her lawyers said on Tuesday that she is receiving medical care while handcuffed in a hospital. She was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995.\n\nLast Wednesday, Pike survived two failed lethal injections in Tennessee. Because the chemicals did not work as planned, she was taken to hospital, where she stayed unconscious for days. Experts say she is believed to be the only person ever to survive a lethal injection. Her lawyers called her recovery 'medically unprecedented'.\n\nDeborah Denno, a criminologist at Fordham Law School, said she was 'absolutely astonished' that Pike is awake. In seven other cases, prisoners survived because executioners could not inject anything into their veins. However, Pike is the only person who actually received a toxin. 'This has never happened before,' Denno said.\n\nAuthorities have not said whether they will try to execute Pike again, and they have not explained what went wrong. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee has suspended all executions for the rest of the year, and the state's prison chief plans to resign. Pike's attorneys will appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday.\n\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said most people die from lethal injection. He warned that many unknowns remain, such as how much pentobarbital entered her system and what her recovery will look like. 'I would not say all the big risks are behind her,' he noted.", "body_zh": "50岁的死囚克里斯塔·派克上周在一次失败的处决中幸存，现在已恢复意识并能说话。尽管她仍处于危急状态，但她的律师周二表示，她正在医院接受治疗，戴着手铐。她因1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默而被判处死刑。\n\n上周三，派克在田纳西州两次注射死刑失败后幸存。由于化学药物没有按计划起作用，她被送往医院，昏迷了数天。专家称，她被认为是唯一一个在注射死刑后幸存的人。她的律师称她的康复是“医学上史无前例的”。\n\n福特汉姆法学院的犯罪学家黛博拉·丹诺说，她对派克清醒并能说话感到“绝对震惊”。在另外七起案件中，囚犯幸存是因为行刑者无法将药物注入他们的静脉。然而，派克是唯一实际接受了毒素的人。丹诺说：“这种情况从未发生过。”\n\n当局尚未表示是否会再次处决派克，也没有解释出了什么问题。田纳西州州长比尔·李已暂停今年剩余时间的所有处决，该州监狱负责人计划辞职。派克的律师将于周三在纳什维尔出庭。\n\n为派克辩护团队提供咨询的麻醉师乔尔·齐沃特博士说，大多数人会死于注射死刑。他警告说，仍有许多未知因素，例如有多少戊巴比妥进入了她的体内，以及她的康复情况会如何。他指出：“我不会说所有重大风险都已过去。”", "text": "Christa Pike, a 50-year-old death row inmate, is now conscious and speaking after she survived a failed execution last week. Although she remains in critical condition, her lawyers said on Tuesday that she is receiving medical care while handcuffed in a hospital. She was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Last Wednesday, Pike survived two failed lethal injections in Tennessee. Because the chemicals did not work as planned, she was taken to hospital, where she stayed unconscious for days. Experts say she is believed to be the only person ever to survive a lethal injection. Her lawyers called her recovery 'medically unprecedented'. Deborah Denno, a criminologist at Fordham Law School, said she was 'absolutely astonished' that Pike is awake. In seven other cases, prisoners survived because executioners could not inject anything into their veins. However, Pike is the only person who actually received a toxin. 'This has never happened before,' Denno said. Authorities have not said whether they will try to execute Pike again, and they have not explained what went wrong. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee has suspended all executions for the rest of the year, and the state's prison chief plans to resign. Pike's attorneys will appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday. Dr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said most people die from lethal injection. He warned that many unknowns remain, such as how much pentobarbital entered her system and what her recovery will look like. 'I would not say all the big risks are behind her,' he noted.", "vocab": [{"word": "death row", "pos": "noun", "zh": "死囚牢房", "note": "指等待处决的囚犯区域"}, {"word": "inmate", "pos": "noun", "zh": "囚犯", "note": "常用于监狱语境"}, {"word": "lethal injection", "pos": "noun", "zh": "注射死刑", "note": "lethal 意为致命的"}, {"word": "execution", "pos": "noun", "zh": "处决", "note": "动词是 execute"}, {"word": "conscious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有意识的", "note": "反义词 unconscious 昏迷的"}, {"word": "unprecedented", "pos": "adj", "zh": "史无前例的", "note": "常用于正式报道"}, {"word": "criminologist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "犯罪学家", "note": "研究犯罪的人"}, {"word": "astonished", "pos": "adj", "zh": "震惊的", "note": "表示非常惊讶"}, {"word": "suspend", "pos": "verb", "zh": "暂停", "note": "常用于官方决定"}, {"word": "anaesthesiologist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "麻醉师", "note": "医学专业词汇"}], "title_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say", "summary_original": "Experts and lawyers called the apparent recovery unprecedented, noting she is believed to be the only known person to survive a lethal injection.", "body_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say\nBy\nSareen Habeshian\nand\nKwasi Gyamfi Asiedu\nPublished\n6 October 2026\nUpdated 57 minutes ago\nUS death row inmate Christa Pike is \"conscious and speaking\" after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, her lawyers say.\nPike, 50, continues to receive critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital, her attorneys said in a statement on Tuesday.\nPike, who was sentenced to death after murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995, survived two failed lethal injections last Wednesday in Tennessee. She was taken to hospital, where she remained unconscious for days as medical staff cleared her body of the injected chemical.\nExperts and her legal team say her apparent recovery is unprecedented. She is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection.\nHer lawyers called her progress \"medically unprecedented\", and while her prognosis remains unclear, \"at a minimum, we expect a long recovery\".\nDeborah Denno, a criminologist and professor at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking.\nThere were seven other cases where prisoners survived slated executions, but in those cases, executioners were not able to inject anything into the inmates' veins, Denno told the BBC.\nPike \"is the only person for whom some kind of toxin has been injected,\" she said.\n\"They did everything they were supposed to do as part of the execution process, and it simply didn't work,\" Denno said. \"This has never happened before.\"\nAuthorities have not yet said whether they will try again to execute Pike. They have also not offered an explanation for what went wrong after injecting her with the chemical pentobarbital.\nTennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year - and the head of prisons in the state said over the weekend that he plans to resign.\nPike was 18 when she and her then-boyfriend, Tadaryl Shipp, beat, tortured and killed 19-year-old Slemmer, whom they had met at a job training camp for troubled teens.\nPike's attorneys are scheduled to appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday. They also plan to hold a news conference outside the court.\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said on Tuesday that the likelihood of recovering from lethal injection is low.\n\"Most people who get lethal injection die from it,\" he told the BBC. \"In fact, pretty well everyone, except Christa. So, the fact that she survived it ... was unusual.\"\nBut there remains a lot of uncertainty and many unknowns, he said, including how much of the pentobarbital got into her system, what her blood levels were after the injection and what her recovery will look like.\n\"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he noted.\nZivot had previously said the two doses of pentobarbital she received last week would have been enough that, had it entered her bloodstream in normal circulation, \"she would have surely died\".\nInstead, Zivot said a possible explanation is that instead of entering Pike's bloodstream, the pentobarbital was more likely to have spread across the tissue under her skin.\nZivot said last week he thought her ending up with a brain injury was \"very possible\", due to the delays in resuscitating her. He also believed it would take about a week to truly understand her condition and do a neurological exam. It's now been six days since the failed attempt to execute her.\nPike's lawyers previously warned that her medical history and anatomy - including thrombocytosis (a blood-clotting condition) and small veins - meant there was a risk she would experience \"unnecessary\" pain and suffering during a lethal injection.\nThey said on Tuesday that she has endured \"severe damage\" to her arms.\nRelated topics\nTennessee\nCapital punishment\nUnited States\nMore on this story\nI interviewed Christa Pike 20 years ago - I can't stop thinking about her\nPublished\n3 days ago\nTennessee prison chief to resign after Christa Pike's failed execution\nPublished\n3 days ago\nWhat happened in the failed execution of Christa Pike - and what next?\nPublished\nJust now", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:57:05.204052", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Christa", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.488, "sm": 100, "em": 487, "cs": 0, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Pike", "s": 0.5, "e": 0.825, "sm": 500, "em": 825, "cs": 8, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 0.825, "e": 1.025, "sm": 825, "em": 1025, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "a", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.087, "sm": 1025, "em": 1087, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "50", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.234, "sm": 1100, "em": 1234, "cs": 16, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "-", "s": 1.234, "e": 1.301, "sm": 1234, "em": 1301, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "year-old", "s": 1.301, "e": 1.838, "sm": 1301, "em": 1837, "cs": 19, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "death", "s": 1.85, "e": 2.1, "sm": 1850, "em": 2100, "cs": 28, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "row", "s": 2.112, "e": 2.262, "sm": 2112, "em": 2262, "cs": 34, "ce": 37, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "inmate", "s": 2.275, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2275, "em": 2750, "cs": 38, "ce": 44, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": ",", "s": 2.75, "e": 3.025, "sm": 2750, "em": 3025, "cs": 44, "ce": 45, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "is", "s": 3.025, "e": 3.137, "sm": 3025, "em": 3137, "cs": 46, "ce": 48, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "now", "s": 3.15, "e": 3.35, "sm": 3150, "em": 3350, "cs": 